1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,650
Static typing in doeff. A type checker follows your effects out to the handler, and back.

2
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:14,800
It checks three things. First, the value each effect answers with.

3
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:19,150
Second, the effects a program may yield.

4
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,500
And third, the value a handler answers with.

5
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:30,800
An effect declares its answer type. ReadClock is an EffectBase of int: its handler answers with an int.

6
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:35,900
A generic parent works too, and the same type can be read at run time: WriteShared answers a bool.

7
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:43,950
An effect on plain EffectBase leaves its answer type unknown: Any.

8
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:49,600
elapsed takes a start time, since, and its result is an int.

9
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:55,550
It reads the clock, reads it again with a bare yield, and returns now minus since.

10
00:00:56,150 --> 00:01:02,950
Yield from an effect: the program pauses, the effect travels out, and the clock handler sends back the answer.

11
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:09,000
The checker knows that answer's type. now is an int, in pyright and in mypy.

12
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:15,300
The bare yield runs exactly the same way, but the checker only sees Any.

13
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:22,950
label runs elapsed with yield from. A sub-program gives its result type: spent is an int.

14
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:32,450
The at-do decorator keeps three things of the function it wraps: its parameters, its effects, and its result.

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,200
The parameters. Calling elapsed with a string is a type error.

16
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:43,300
The effects. Yielding an effect outside the declared set is a type error too.

17
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:48,750
And the result. Running the program under its handler gives an int.

18
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,300
A handler answers an effect by resuming k, the rest of the program, with a value.

19
00:01:57,850 --> 00:02:02,683
typed resume checks that value against the effect's answer type.

20
00:02:02,683 --> 00:02:06,850
One thousand is an int, so elapsed returns six hundred.

21
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:11,350
Answering ReadClock with a string is refused by the checker.

22
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:17,017
A handler that no effect can reach is refused twice: by the checker,

23
00:02:17,017 --> 00:02:19,550
and by the handler decorator when it runs.

24
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:26,133
The same types can be read at run time, so tools that cannot run pyright,

25
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:29,300
such as the Hy checker, read one source of truth.

26
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:37,650
What is not typed: Ask and Get answer Any, because the environment and the state are dynamic.

27
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:42,767
And whether the handlers cover a program's effects is not a type error.

28
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:46,250
Without the clock handler, run raises UnhandledEffect.

29
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:53,450
In doeff, effects carry their types. The checker follows them out to the handler, and back.
